content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite dosed)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.4 mm/s: the limit is the HF-300 severity chart (Figure 3, mm/s RMS on bearing housings). 3.4 mm/s falls in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s), 'Long-term operation'. It is below the Zone C 'plan maintenance' boundary of 4.5 mm/s and the Zone D 'stop the pump' boundary of 7.1 mm/s. Stopping is not required on vibration grounds. Classification should use the highest reading of the two bearing housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 70 C: the limit is the manual specification of normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C, measured on the housing surface. The reading is at the top of the normal band, below alarm and trip, but has no margin left. Monitor the trend.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal drip of about one drop per second: no documented leakage acceptance limit is provided. The manual troubleshooting table treats leakage at the shaft seal as a fault, with corrective action to replace the mechanical seal and check alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall condition: no reading reaches a documented stop or trip criterion. A planned seal replacement is justified by the active leak on a chemically dosed line. The pump is also in the serial range affected by a known early seal failure issue.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C13",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. This is most likely because the pump (serial HF3-22871) is in the range of SB-2026-014, which reports early failure of component seal HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000 due to a revised sleeve tolerance. This applies if an HF3-450 is still fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is listed as a cause of seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature. The vibration (Zone B) and the temperature (at the 70 C normal limit) are both elevated, which is consistent with misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry, for example through loss of the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge. The seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or over-greasing, as a contributor to the 70 C housing temperature and the vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Plan the job as a seal replacement under SB-2026-014. Confirm the serial (HF3-22871 is at or above HF3-22000). Issue cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, record vibration on both bearing housings and record the housing temperature as a baseline. Classify the highest vibration reading against Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. No sleeve setting measurement is needed for the pre-set HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B and a new casing gasket HF3-120. The gasket must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Torque the fasteners with lightly oiled threads: seal gland nuts (M10) to 30 Nm per SB-2026-014, not the 25 Nm in Table 5. Impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm. Casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm. Bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, check the bearing grease quantity and inspect both bearings. If either shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both (HF3-512 drive end and HF3-510 non-drive end) as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out laser shaft alignment after reassembly to tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular. This is required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and is also the recommended check for seal leakage and vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in place. Make sure the casing is full and vented so the seal does not run dry on start-up.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After return to service, re-measure vibration on both bearing housings and the housing temperature. Confirm vibration is no worse than Zone B (4.5 mm/s or below), temperature is no higher than 70 C, and there is no seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, replace whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency only: fit if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is on the filtered-water line, which is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Treat the seal leakage and drained fluid as chemically contaminated (see open questions for the controls required).",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal must never run dry. Confirm the Plan 11 flush and fill the pump before start-up.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not apply the previous shift's instruction to use 25 Nm on all pumps. For this serial, the gland nut torque is 30 Nm per SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours, 2 technicians (standard time).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency, only if bearings are found worn: bearing replacement (pair), 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: the manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, and SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. P-104 is serial HF3-22871, which is above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and the torque is 30 Nm. The previous shift's note that 25 Nm is correct for all pumps is wrong; 25 Nm applies only to pumps below HF3-22000 using HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list gives HF3-450 (component seal), and SB-2026-014 says do NOT fit HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above, use HF3-450B instead. HF3-450B applies to P-104 because of its serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling: manual procedure 5.2 requires sleeve inspection. The bulletin states HF3-450B is pre-set with no sleeve measurement needed, but the sleeve must still be replaced if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. Both apply: inspect for scoring against the 0.1 mm criterion, but no seal setting measurement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No documented acceptance limit for seal leakage rate (about one drop per second) is provided, so how urgent the leak is cannot be measured against a limit.",
    "Which seal is currently fitted to P-104 (original HF3-450 or HF3-450B) is not stated. This affects whether the SB-2026-014 failure mode is the likely cause.",
    "The required PPE, chemical isolation, flushing and leak containment controls for sodium hypochlorite service (Westfield SSP-07) are not included in the evidence beyond the statement that the line is dosed.",
    "It is not stated which bearing housing the 3.4 mm/s and 70 C readings were taken on, or whether 3.4 mm/s is the highest of the two housings. Previous readings and trend are also not provided.",
    "Torque values for fasteners other than the gland nuts on the HF3-450B cartridge seal (for example, cartridge set screws or locking clips) are not given in the bulletin.",
    "Standard labour time is given for mechanical seal replacement generally. It is not confirmed whether the HF3-450B cartridge seal changes this time.",
    "Whether removing the back pull-out assembly disturbs the motor or bearing housing enough to require realignment is not explicitly stated. Alignment is recommended here as a precaution and as a diagnostic step.",
    "It is not confirmed whether SB-2026-014 has been revised or superseded since 14 March 2026.",
    "Stock availability of HF3-450B, HF3-120 and HF3-455, and of bearings HF3-512 and HF3-510 if needed, is not known."
  ]
}
